# Engine API requests (module-agnostic). They go through the gateway: start everything with the AppHost
#   dotnet run --project backend/src/AppHost/Flowgent.AppHost
# To call the engine service directly (no gateway), use http://localhost:5081.
#
# The run examples use the template module (modules/_template), disabled by default:
#   dotnet run --project backend/src/AppHost/Flowgent.AppHost -- --AppHost:Modules:template:Enabled=true
# Any workflow listed by GET /api/engine/workflows works: change @WorkflowId and the request body.
# Paste a run id returned by "Submit an input" into @RunId.

@HostAddress = http://localhost:5080
@WorkflowId = template-hello
@RunId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Runtime configuration (sequential mode, Demo mode, LLM provider and model; never secrets)

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/engine/config

### Modules with availability and validation errors

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/engine/modules

### Workflows (graph, input schema, samples), optionally filtered by module

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/engine/workflows

### One workflow

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/engine/workflows/{{WorkflowId}}

### Published JSON Schema of the workflow format (module, workflow, samples)

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/engine/schemas/workflow

### Submit an input (202 with messageId and runId; 400 when the input does not match the input schema)

POST {{HostAddress}}/api/engine/workflows/{{WorkflowId}}/runs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "Flowgent runs workflows described in YAML. Each module publishes its definitions and tools, and the engine runs them."
}

### Submit an invalid input (400 problem details with the workflow's errorMessage and per-field errors)

POST {{HostAddress}}/api/engine/workflows/{{WorkflowId}}/runs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "   "
}

### Runs, newest first (filters: moduleId, workflowId, status, limit)

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/engine/runs?workflowId={{WorkflowId}}&limit=20

### Runs awaiting input

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/engine/runs?status=AwaitingInput

### One run (input, step outputs, final output)

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/engine/runs/{{RunId}}

### Abort a run (202 running, 204 queued, 404 unknown, 409 already completed)

POST {{HostAddress}}/api/engine/runs/{{RunId}}/abort

### Pending human inputs with their review payload (filters: moduleId, workflowId)

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/engine/human-inputs

### Approve a run awaiting input (204, 404, 409)

POST {{HostAddress}}/api/engine/human-inputs/{{RunId}}/approve

### Reject a run awaiting input, with an optional reason (204, 404, 409)

POST {{HostAddress}}/api/engine/human-inputs/{{RunId}}/reject
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Needs a different approach."
}

### Transition events, newest first (filters: moduleId, workflowId, runId, limit; max 200)

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/engine/events?limit=50

### Agents of all modules with status (Idle/Working)

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/engine/agents

### LLM telemetry of one agent

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/engine/agents/template_writer/telemetry

### Global LLM usage (optionally per module)

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/engine/telemetry/summary

### Inbox messages (status: queued, processed, failed; moduleId)

GET {{HostAddress}}/api/engine/inbox?status=queued

### Engine health (direct call, not routed by the gateway)

GET http://localhost:5081/health
